# TypeScript + oxlint anti-slop

Lint is **oxlint** (`npm run lint`), plugin `tools/oxlint/anti-slop`. Config: `oxlint.config.ts`. Typecheck: `npm run check`.

## Banned patterns (error)

- `typeof` runtime checks → `anti-slop/no-runtime-typeof`
- `unknown` params / returns / aliases
- `any`, chained assertions, widen-then-assert
- Bare `object` parameters and unsafe `Record` dictionaries
- Module mocking patterns the plugin flags

## Boundary decoding

Use `$lib/parse` instead of `typeof` / `unknown`:

- `UntypedInput` / `JsonValue` / `JsonObject`
- `isStringValue`, `isPlainObject`, `readString`, `readFiniteNumber`, `parseJsonValue`, `readProcessEnv`

At I/O edges, parse into a named domain type, then use that type inward.

## Assertions

If a type assertion is unavoidable, put a `// SAFETY:` comment on the preceding line explaining why it is sound (see `parseJsonValue` and the Convex token fetch in `+layout.svelte`). Do not add SAFETY comments to silence the rule.

## Convex / Svelte interop

Generated `src/convex/_generated/**` is ignored by oxlint. Do not disable anti-slop in app source to match Convex guideline snippets that use `typeof` or `unknown` — adapt those snippets to `$lib/parse`.
